@startuml
title FEQ-D01 Fiscal Exception Queue System Context
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Support / Compliance\nUsers" as Users

component "Central PMS\npayment finality, fiscal references,\nnormal ExitAuthorization" as Central
component "Fiscal Exception Queue\nrecovery coordination" as FEQ
component "POS Server\nfiscal issuance and numbering" as POS
component "Operator Console\nvisibility / governed handoff" as OC
component "Management Dashboard\nvisibility / reporting" as MDR
component "Audit / Event" as Audit
component "Reconciliation" as Recon
component "Gate / Exit\nthrough Central PMS authorization" as Gate

Users --> OC : view/assign/escalate\nwhere permitted
Users --> FEQ : governed recovery actions\nthrough approved service path
Central --> FEQ : detected fiscal exception\nand fiscal reference state
FEQ --> Central : update exception workflow\nand fiscal reference outcome
FEQ --> POS : approved backend\nGET readback / retry call
POS --> FEQ : fiscal issuance evidence\nor failure/conflict
FEQ --> Audit : attempts, decisions,\nassignments, closure
FEQ --> Recon : reconciliation status\nand closure evidence
FEQ --> OC : assigned exception\nvisibility
FEQ --> MDR : projection/reporting\nupdates
Central --> Gate : normal ExitAuthorization\nonly when eligible

OC -[#red,dashed]-> POS : no direct POS Server call
MDR -[#red,dashed]-> POS : no direct POS Server call
FEQ -[#red,dashed]-> Gate : no gate command

note bottom
Central PMS owns fiscal reference state and normal ExitAuthorization.
POS Server owns fiscal issuance/numbering.
FEQ coordinates recovery through approved backend services.
end note
@enduml
